    & V(u):& G \to \mathcal{H}, \quad x \mapsto \rho(x)(u), \quad \forall x \in G.
    \end{eqnarray}

\label{gowers-hatami-2}

Let \(G\) be a finite group, \(\varepsilon \geq 0\), and \(\rho: G \rightarrow U(\mathcal{H})\) an \((\varepsilon, \sigma)\)-representation of \(G\) on space $\mathcal{H}=\mathbb{C}^{d}$. 
Then there exists an isometry \(V: \mathcal{H} \rightarrow \mathcal{H}^\prime\) to a different space $\mathcal{H}^\prime$, 
and a representation \(\rho^\prime: G \rightarrow \mathcal{H}^\prime\) such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}_{x \in G}\left\|\rho(x)-V^{*} \rho^\prime(x) V\right\|_{\sigma}^{2} \leq 2 \varepsilon.
\end{equation}



A regular-representation proof of the Gowers-Hatami theorem appears in Morel's slides~\cite{Morel20}, following the original Gowers-Hatami theorem~\cite{GowHat17}.

The rest of the proof follows by expanding the $\sigma$-norm, bounding the norm of $\mathbb{E}_{x \in G} V^* \rho^\prime(x) V$ and applying the definition of $(\varepsilon, \sigma)$-representation.
 In particular, we have 
 \begin{eqnarray}
    & &\mathbb{E}_{x \in G}\left\|\rho(x)-V^{*} \rho^\prime(x) V\right\|_{\sigma}^{2} \\ 
    &= & \mathbb{E}_{x \in G} \| \rho(x) \|_\sigma^2 + \mathbb{E}_{x \in G} \|V^* \rho^\prime(x) V\|_\sigma^2 - 2 \mathbb{E}_{x \in G} \Re \langle \rho(x), V^* \rho^\prime(x) V\rangle_\sigma \nonumber
\end{eqnarray}        

Because $\rho$ is unitary and ${\rm Tr} \sigma = 1$, $\mathbb{E}_{x \in G} \| \rho(x) \|_\sigma^2 = 1$.
For the second term, recall from Eq.~\eqref{eq:isometry-average} that the compression is the group average $V^* \rho^\prime(x) V = \mathbb{E}_{y \in G} \rho^*(y)\rho(yx)$. Each summand $\rho^*(y)\rho(yx)$ is a product of unitaries, hence unitary, so $\|\rho^*(y)\rho(yx)\|_\sigma = 1$. By convexity of the $\sigma$-norm---the triangle inequality applied to the average---we obtain
\begin{equation} \label{eq:isometry-unitary-bound}
\|V^* \rho^\prime(x) V\|_\sigma = \left\| \mathbb{E}_{y \in G} \rho^*(y)\rho(yx) \right\|_\sigma \le \mathbb{E}_{y \in G} \|\rho^*(y)\rho(yx)\|_\sigma = 1,
\end{equation}
hence $\mathbb{E}_{x \in G}\|V^* \rho^\prime(x) V\|_\sigma^2 \le 1$.

Therefore using the bounds in ~Eq.~\eqref{eq:isometry-unitary-bound} and ~Eq.~\eqref{eq:inner-product-bound} by applying Lemma~\ref{gowers-hatami-correlation}, we have
\begin{equation}
